First, let's use the Law of Sines in triangles $BAD$ and $DAE$:

\begin{align*}
\frac{BD}{\sin x} &= \frac{AD}{\sin (180 - x - y)} \\
\frac{DE}{\sin y} &= \frac{AE}{\sin (180 - y - z)}
\end{align*}

Since $BD = DE$ (because they are both equal to $EC)$, we have:

\begin{align*}
\frac{AD}{\sin (180 - x - y)} &= \frac{AE}{\sin (180 - y - z)} \\
\text{or,} & \frac{AD}{AE} = \frac{\sin (180 - y - z)}{\sin (180 - x - y)} \\
\text{or,} & \frac{\sin (x + y)}{\sin z} = \frac{AD}{AE}
\end{align*}

Now, we can use the Law of Sines in triangle $ACE$ to find the ratio of $AE$ to $AC$:

\begin{align*}
\frac{EC}{\sin z} &= \frac{AC}{\sin (180 - z - x)}
\end{align*}

Multiply the two ratios $\frac{\sin (x + y)}{\sin z}$ and $\frac{AC}{AE}$:

\begin{align*}
\frac{\sin (x + y)}{\sin z} \cdot \frac{AC}{AE} &= \frac{\sin (x + y) \sin (180 - z - x)}{\sin z \sin x} \\
\text{or,} & \frac{\sin (180 - z - x)}{\sin x} \\
\text{or,} & \frac{\sin (z + x)}{\sin x}
\end{align*}

Since the area of triangle $ABC$ is $\frac{1}{2} AC \times BE$, we can write:

\begin{align*}
\text{area }ABC &= \frac{1}{2} AC \times BE \\
&= \frac{1}{2} AE \times EC + \frac{1}{2} AD \times DE \\
&= \frac{1}{2} AE \times EC + \frac{1}{2} AD \times AD \\
\text{or,} & \text{area }ABC = \frac{1}{2} AE \times EC + \frac{1}{2} AD^2 \sin y
\end{align*}

Now, we can find the factor $\frac{\text{area }ABC}{AE \times EC}$:

\begin{align*}
\frac{\text{area }ABC}{AE \times EC} &= \frac{1}{2} \cdot \frac{AD^2 \sin y}{AE \cdot EC} \\
&= \frac{1}{2} \cdot \frac{AD^2}{AE^2} \cdot \frac{\sin y}{EC} \\
\text{or,} & \frac{1}{2} \cdot \left(\frac{\sin y}{EC}\right) \cdot \left(\frac{BD}{\sin y}\right)^2 \\
\text{or,} & \frac{1}{2} \cdot \left(\frac{\sin y}{EC}\right) \cdot \left(\frac{\sin x + \sin y}{\sin y}\right)^2 \\
\text{or,} & \frac{1}{2} \cdot \left(\frac{\sin x + \sin y}{\sin y}\right) \cdot \frac{\sin (x + y)}{\sin z}
\end{align*}

Finally, we can find the expression for $\frac{\sin (x + y) \sin (y + z)}{\sin x \sin z}$:

\begin{align*}
\frac{\sin (x + y) \sin (y + z)}{\sin x \sin z} &= \left(\frac{1}{2} \cdot \left(\frac{\sin x + \sin y}{\sin y}\right) \cdot \frac{\text{area }ABC}{AE \times EC}\right)^{-1} \\
&= 2 \cdot \frac{\sin x \sin z}{\sin (x + y)} \cdot \frac{AE \times EC}{\text{area }ABC} \\
&= 2 \cdot \frac{\sin x \sin z}{\sin (x + y)} \cdot \frac{AC}{\frac{1}{2} AE \times EC + \frac{1}{2} AD^2 \sin y}
\end{align*}
