We start by calculating the total number of possible outcomes when rolling six 6-sided dice:

The number of outcomes for rolling a single 6-sided die is 6^1 = 6.
When we roll six dice simultaneously, the number of outcomes becomes:
\boxed{ 6^6 = 46,656 }

Next, we need to find the number of outcomes for all the dice showing at least one 1 or at least one 2:

1) The chances of rolling a 1 on a single die is 1/6. Finding the total number of outcomes when rolling one or more 1s on 6 dice:
\boxed{ \binom{6}{1} * ((1/6) * (5/6)^5) + \binom{6}{2} * ((1/6)^2) * (5/6)^4 + ... + (1/6)^6 }

2) Similarly, the chances of rolling a 2 on a single die is also 1/6. Finding the total number of outcomes when rolling one or more 2s on 6 dice:
\boxed{ \binom{6}{1} * ((1/6) * (5/6)^5) + \binom{6}{2} * ((1/6)^2) * (5/6)^4 + ... + (1/6)^6 }

Add both results to calculate the desired probability:
\boxed{ \left[ \boxed{ \binom{6}{1} * ((1/6) * (5/6)^5) + \binom{6}{2} * ((1/6)^2) * (5/6)^4 + ... + (1/6)^6 } + \boxed{ \binom{6}{1} * ((1/6) * (5/6)^5) + \binom{6}{2} * ((1/6)^2) * (5/6)^4 + ... + (1/6)^6 } \right] \div 46656 \text{ or } \boxed{\left[ \frac{259,214,496}{46,656^2} + \frac{259,214,496}{46,656^2} \right] \div 46656} }

