Using the formula for the surface area of a cylinder $A = 2\pi r(L + r)$, we can find the lateral surface area of the tube:
\begin{align}
\text{Lateral Surface Area} = 2\pi r \left( L + r \right) &= 2\pi (0.006) \left( L + 0.006 \right) &\text{(substituting given values)}\\
&= 0.12\pi \left( L + 0.006 \right) &\text{(multiplication)}\\
&= 0.12\pi L + 0.0072\pi &\text{(distributive property)}\\
\end{align}

The volume of the cylindrical tube can be found using the formula $V = \pi r^2 L$.
\begin{align}
\text{Volume} &= \pi r^2 L &= \pi (0.006)^2 L &\text{(substituting given values)}\\
&= 0.00072\pi L &\text{(multiplication)}
\end{align}

Since we were asked to find the tube's volume and express the answer in terms of $\pi$, we can simply write the verified volume expression above (without the $L$ since it's unknown):
\begin{align}
\boxed{0.00072 \pi} \text{ cubic centimeters}
\end{align}

