To solve the problem:
1. Wendy has \(5\) quarters left over after stacking the first time.
2. Rand then stacks quarters, and Wendy has \(5\) quarters left over again.
3. The combined amount of quarters that Wendy has is the initial amount she had minus twice the number of quarters left over: \( \text{quarters} = \text{initial} - 2 \times \text{left over} \).
