z^4 + (1+e^{i\left(\frac{2\pi}{3}\right)})z^3 + p_2z^2 + p_1z + p_0 &= (z-e^{i\left(\frac{2\pi}{3}\right)})^3(z-r_4) \\
\implies z^4 +e^{i\left(\frac{2\pi}{3} + \theta\right)}z^3 + p_2z^2 + p_1z + p_0 &= (z-e^{i\left(\frac{2\pi}{3}\right)})^3(z-r_4)
\end{align*}

We need to solve for $\theta$. This can be done by comparing the coefficient of $z^3$ on both sides of the equation:
\begin{align*}
e^{i\left(\frac{2\pi}{3} + \theta\right)} &= 1 + e^{i\left(\frac{2\pi}{3}\right)} \\
\implies \theta &= -\frac{2\pi}{3}
\end{align*}

However, the angle between $90^\circ$ and $180^\circ$ is not in the range $[0^\circ, 360^\circ)$. Instead, we can apply wrapping at multiples of $360^\circ$ to the answer to get: $\theta = -\frac{2\pi}{3} + 360^\circ = 330^\circ$.

\boxed{330^\circ}

